{"type":"message","id":"20a73dd2","parentId":"cd2eed29","timestamp":"2026-07-28T07:02:00.097Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes — token usage data is available and being captured.**\n\nHere's where it comes from:\n\n1. **Session-level `.jsonl` files** — Every agent session writes to `~/.openclaw/agents/<agent>/sessions/*.jsonl`. Each message in these files includes a `usage` field with:\n   - `input` / `output` tokens\n   - `cacheRead` / `cacheWrite` tokens\n   - `totalTokens`\n   - `cost` object\n\n2. **`aggregate_run_tokens.py`** — This script scans all agent session logs, finds entries referencing the run directory, aggregates tokens by model, computes USD cost from pricing in `openclaw.json`, and writes:\n   - `$RUN_DIR/publish/tokens.json` — detailed breakdown\n   - Manifest `results.tokens` field\n\n3. **`picked_stories` table** — Token totals are stored via `update_pick_status.py`:\n   - `tokens_in`, `tokens_out`, `tokens_total`\n   - `tokens_by_model` (JSON)\n   - `cost_usd`\n\n**In this run**, no tokens were recorded because:\n- The story failed at the topic-duplicate check (Step 2.1) before reaching Step 2.6 where `aggregate_run_tokens.py` runs\n- The picker and researcher sessions show **zero tokens** (`\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,...}`) — likely Bedrock-mantle isn't reporting actual token counts to the session log\n\nThe schema is there and working for other runs (your DB shows historical token data like 342K in / 28K out per story). The issue is likely the Bedrock provider not populating the usage fields, not the pipeline itself."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1785222112099,"responseId":"chatcmpl-6abcd0d7-7810-4ca6-8225-1379c9a72b5f"}}
